vulnerabilities.suggested_fix:
Either revert when the module returns a fee above the maximum allowed threshold, or raise the factory's fee ceiling to match the module's cap. Additionally, emit an event when an out-of-range fee is encountered so operators can detect and correct misconfigurations. Example fix:

```solidity
function getSwapFee(address pool) external view override returns (uint24) {
    if (swapFeeModule != address(0)) {
        (bool success, bytes memory data) = swapFeeModule.excessivelySafeStaticCall(
            200_000, 32, abi.encodeWithSelector(IFeeModule.getFee.selector, pool)
        );
        if (success) {
            uint24 fee = abi.decode(data, (uint24));
            require(fee <= maxSwapFee, "Fee exceeds maximum");
            return fee;
        }
    }
    return tickSpacingToFee[CLPool(pool).tickSpacing()];
}
```
